ZoneSDK is a fan-made source library for building ReShade add-ons for
S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2: Heart of Chornobyl. It is not made, approved, sponsored or
endorsed by GSC Game World and is not affiliated with GSC Game World.
S.T.A.L.K.E.R. and S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2: Heart of Chornobyl are trademarks of
their respective owners and are named here only to say which game ZoneSDK
works with.

Game data
---------

ZoneSDK contains no game files and no game assets: no game executables or
parts of them, no packaged game content, models, textures, sounds, maps or
game texts. It contains only the facts an add-on needs at run time to work
together with the running game (interoperability):

- short masked search patterns: short runs of machine-code bytes in which the
  variable positions are masked out, used to find engine structures in the
  memory of the running game;
- short byte checks and addresses (offsets from the image base) for specific,
  identified game builds, used to confirm a known build before a feature that
  depends on it is switched on;
- names and parameter layouts of engine functions, classes and properties
  (data/builds/<build>/ufunctions.txt, build.json and proven.txt).

ZoneSDK does not ship, change or redistribute game files. On a game build it
does not recognise, an add-on switches the affected features off.

Third-party code
----------------

The ReShade add-on API headers (extern/reshade), the Dear ImGui headers
(extern/imgui) and the stb headers that ship with Dear ImGui keep their own
licences. See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt and extern/LICENSES. Every add-on built
with ZoneSDK should carry NOTICE-ADDON.txt.
